      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 19-year-old youth with known right cryptorchidism had repeated attacks of acute abdominal symptoms, previously transient but now intensifying. Surgical exploration revealed a gangrenous intra-abdominal testis, which was successfully removed. Histologic examination confirmed the diagnosis of torsion."},
